Z||000022||fropuff||01-14-2001||12:19 AM||||Nice frickin car!!!  I really like the idea of the 5.25 in the center console.  I was wondering if you could please give me some more information about it, and maybe some more pictures.  How does it add to the sound?  I was thinking of putting an 8 under the dash or in a floor box and getting one for the center console.  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000023||RiceCooker||01-15-2001||02:10 PM||||Alright, I'm starting to feel a bit better.<P>Cheever: DREAM ON!!<P>Fropuff: I wish I had more pics but I only borrowed a digital camera for one day and it was after the install. I don't have a scanner either. If you have taken apart the center console you will be able to understand this. I made a speaker enclosure out of wood in this shape:<BR>l---l<BR>l O l<BR>l---l<BR> That looks bad but the circle in the middle should be bigger cuase the speaker mounts flush onto that, then i fastned it from both sides to the basket shaped part of the center console.<P>The front part of the center console was a real bagbiter. There's no easy way to cut a circle through it and it's not pretty either. The size of the grill is just traced and cut out and then I popped the grill in - it's not attached to the speeaker. <P>I've had a lot of comments on the looks and I can open the console and look down to the speaker. I also covered the top with plexiglass so there is some room in there for keys, papers, etc.<P>As for sound, I'm not too sure. My reasoning, is the more speakers the better. It's not a true center channel just mono (bridged L/R) It definitley adds to the sound but it might not win me any competition trophies. As far as I know, Oreif seems to be the audio whiz kid of the forum so you're probably a lot better asking him any technical questions about audio staging etc etc. (I don't even know what I just said)<P>Anything else, just ask<BR>Todd||||reg||6
